<item><title>Molapo wins November Golf Corporate League tournament</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ls/molapo-wins-november-golf-corporate-league-tournament-7455a8/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ls/molapo-wins-november-golf-corporate-league-tournament-7455a8/</guid><category>Lesotho</category><description>Mathaleha Molapo secured first place on countback with 39 points in the Maseru Golf Club Corporate League tournament.</description><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:06:26 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ls.jpg" length="31810" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ls.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Khutlisi elected Maseru mayor after closely contested vote</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ls/khutlisi-elected-maseru-mayor-after-closely-contested-vote-f27641/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ls/khutlisi-elected-maseru-mayor-after-closely-contested-vote-f27641/</guid><category>Lesotho</category><description>Councillor &apos;Malerato Khutlisi won 11 votes to eight against former mayor Thabo Sefuthi at the Maseru City Council chambers.</description><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:06:19 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ls.jpg" length="31810" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ls.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
